      "id": "lixg2cj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Battle of Plassey (1757)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Battle of Plassey (1757) laid the foundation of British rule in India after Robert Clive defeated Nawab Siraj-ud-Daulah.",
        "The Battle of Buxar (1764) saw the defeat of the combined forces of Mir Qasim, Shuja-ud-Daula, and Shah Alam II, establishing British political supremacy.",
        "The Treaty of Allahabad (1765) granted Diwani (revenue collection) rights of Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa to the East India Company.",
        "The Subsidiary Alliance system introduced by Lord Wellesley forced Indian rulers to accept British troops and lose control over foreign affairs.",
        "The Doctrine of Lapse introduced by Lord Dalhousie annexed princely states whose rulers died without a natural male heir."
      ],
      "id": "e9grxco"
    },
